<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrtus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murtus</span></b> ), i and ūs, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a myrtle, myrtle-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 15,
				29, 37, § 122</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viridi caput impedire myrto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 4, 9</span></i>
			.—<b>Poet.</b>, for <i>a spear of myrtle-wood</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et pastoralem praefixā cuspide
					myrtum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 817</span></i>
			.—<i>Nom. plur.</i> myrtūs,
				<i><span class="en">Verg.
				G. 2, 64</span></i>.—As <i>masc.</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
			8</span></i>.—Anteclass. also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">myrta</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murta</span></b> ,
				ae, f.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murta nigra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 125</span></i>
			.—Murtus for  myrtus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">murti nigrae baccae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 109</span></i>
			.</div>
